            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI can not reproduce (both with version of nightly from the issue and 0.9.4):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/24854248/2c7176aa-ce42-414e-93ee-60b56d11624a\r\n\r\nCouple of follow up questions and observations:\r\n- Did you actually reproduce with the minimal setup from the issue? If not, please do that by creating a separate config in `~/.config/nvim-neotree-statusline` and run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-neotree-statusline nvim` (assuming UNIX, otherwise see `:h $NVIM_APPNAME`).\r\n- `StatusLine` highlight group is cleared inside `blocked_filetypes` conditional, but not reinstated afterwards. This might cause an unexpected issue later.\r\n- `filesystem.follow_current_file` in 'neo-tree' is [soft deprecated](https://github.com/nvim-neo-tree/neo-tree.nvim/blob/2f2d08894bbc679d4d181604c16bb7079f646384/lua/neo-tree/defaults.lua#L521-L525) and should be replaced with `filesystem.follow_current_file = { enabled = true }`.\r\n- The fact that statusline shows file path instead of `''` or normal active content means that it shows content from `config.content.inactive`. Thus this should not be an issue with \"disabled\" statusline, but more with that something obstructs how 'mini.statusline' decided which content to show.",
